# Everything git detects as text is stored with LF, whatever the working copy
# uses. Files edited on Windows arrive with CRLF, and committing them as-is turns
# a one-line change into a whole-file diff. First, so the rules below refine it.
* text=auto

# Keep Go sources as LF in the repo and on checkout, on every OS.
# Without this, a Windows checkout (autocrlf) reintroduces CRLF and `gofmt -l`
# flags every file, failing the CI gofmt gate. (.sh is worth adding too if the
# smoke script ever ships CRLF.)
*.go text eol=lf
